# Component conventions

## File & export naming

- Filenames are kebab-case: `chat-bubble.tsx`, `reminder-template-card.tsx`.
- Exports are PascalCase named exports: `export function ChatBubble(...) {}`.
- One component per file. Colocated helpers are fine only if < ~20 lines.

## Primitives

- Import text/view primitives from `@/components/ui/themed-text` and
  `@/components/ui/themed-view`. Never redefine or duplicate them.
- For repeated UI patterns, reach for existing `ui/` primitives first
  (`Card`, `Chip`, `IconBadge`, `GradientButton`, `SectionHeader`,
  `ScreenContainer`, `ProgressRing`, `Collapsible`).

## Design tokens (no hardcoded values)

Import from `@/constants/theme` instead of writing literals:

```ts
import { Brand, Gradients, Shadows } from '@/constants/theme';

// Bad
backgroundColor: '#1E88FF'
shadowOpacity: 0.32

// Good
backgroundColor: Brand.primary
...Shadows.userBubble
colors={Gradients.send}
```

Available tokens: `Brand.{primary, primaryDark, primaryOn, userBubbleTop,
userBubbleBottom, userBubbleShadow, sendShadow, success, warn, warnAmber,
danger, info, violet, violetDark, indigo, heroNavy, heroNavyDeep, heroBlue,
heroBlueDeep}`, `Gradients.{send, composerPrimary, lightboxBackdrop}`,
`Shadows.{assistantBubble, userBubble, composer}`.

## Styling

- Prefer NativeWind `className` utilities for layout/typography/color.
- Use `style={...}` only for dynamic tokens (`Brand`, `Gradients`,
  `Shadows`) or animated values. Never hardcode hex colors.
- Full rule: [styling.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/styling.mdc).

## Platform

- iOS-only app. Use `SymbolView`, `BlurView`, and iOS shadow props
  directly. Do **not** add `.native.tsx` / `.web.tsx` splits or branch on
  `Platform.OS === 'web' | 'android'`. Full rule:
  [ios-only.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ios-only.mdc).
